A||N||11||Bluebottlejunky||Clutch Bleeding? Witch way?||||4||
Z||000000||Bluebottlejunky||06-04-2001||06:57 PM||||Ok, I have heard one too many ways of bleeding the clucth on my 4sp..So what really is the best method?  Thanks, P.S what is the exact size of the bleeder screw bolt?<P><P>------------------<BR>Hello, My name is Mike and I am addicted too fiero's...PLEASE dont help me.<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||4
Z||000001||PBJ||06-04-2001||07:28 PM||||This from the GM service manual.<P>1. unscrew bleed screw at slave cylinder enough to allow fluid to be pumped out (half a turn is normally sufficient)<P>2. push pedal down through full stroke.<P>3. allow pedal to return quickly to its stop by removing foot from the clutch pedal<P>4. repeat procedure until air is dispelled at bleedscrew.<P>5. close bleedscrew immediately after last downward stroke of pedal when air bubbles no longer appear.<P>use dot 3 brake fluid.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bluebottlejunky||06-04-2001||08:27 PM||||Hey PBJ, about how many times normaly do I need to repeat it?<P>------------------<BR>Hello, My name is Mike and I am addicted too fiero's...PLEASE dont help me.<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||10
Z||000003||PBJ||06-04-2001||08:45 PM||||NORMALLY how many times to bleed a fiero clutch? How long do you have? How strong is your left leg?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>Just don't let the reservoir go dry and wait until no more bubbles are present. <P>I would guess that 10 would be sufficient and certainly not more than 15.  BUT if it doesn't feel right let it sit, or if you can drive it and try later.<P>Did your level go low, Did you have a leak, or a component replacement?? I have found that usually they tend to do in pairs. ie clutch master and slave rebuild at the same time.<BR>||||reg||1
